    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27430" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maccus</span></b> , i, m.
		cf. Sanscr. mūkas, dumb; Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μῶκος</span>, mockery; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μῶμος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a buffoon, punchinello, macaroni</i>, in the
			Atellane plays: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in Atellana Oscae personae inducuntur, ut
					maccus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Diom. p. 488</span></i>
			 P.; cf. <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			2621</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a simpleton,
				blockhead</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">macci et buccones,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 325, 30</span></i>
			.</div>
